# =============================================================================
# GHOSTTY CONFIG (Linux) — installed to ~/.config/ghostty/config
# =============================================================================
#
# RELOAD / EDIT THIS FILE
#   ctrl+shift+,        Reload config (applies changes without restarting)
#   ctrl+,              Open config in your editor (Ghostty default)
#   After editing in the repo: make configs, then reload as above.
#   List every active binding: ghostty +list-keybinds
#
# TMUX INTEGRATION
#   Alt is already sent to apps as Meta on Linux, so tmux bindings like
#   Alt+l / Alt+j / Alt+1..9 work without any remapping. Prefix is Ctrl+a.
#
# COMMON GHOSTTY DEFAULTS (Linux)
#   ctrl+shift+t        New tab
#   ctrl+shift+w        Close tab
#   ctrl+shift+n        New window
#   ctrl+shift+o        Split right
#   ctrl+shift+e        Split down
#   ctrl+shift+[ / ]    Previous / next split
#   ctrl+shift+c / v    Copy / paste
#   ctrl+shift+f        Search scrollback
#   ctrl+l              Clear screen
#   ctrl+= / ctrl+-     Increase / decrease font size
#   ctrl+0              Reset font size
#
# Full default list: https://ghostty.org/docs/config/keybind
# =============================================================================
